    "body": "### Motivation\n- Provide reproducible code and analyses requested by reviewers including an explicit ESM2 checkpoint declaration, a ProtT5 embedding comparison, additional baseline models, data-balance experiments, and interpretability reports. \n- Confirm and document the exact ESM2 checkpoint used for embeddings to support Methods edits: `facebook/esm2_t33_650M_UR50D` (default in `embed_esm2.py`).\n- Supply runnable, repo-consistent utilities so heavy compute (embeddings, full benchmarks, active-learning reruns) can be reproduced on appropriate compute nodes.\n\n### Description\n- Added `code/AI_CHEM_code/extract_prot_t5_embeddings.py` to extract mean-pooled ProtT5 embeddings from `Rostlab/prot_t5_xl_uniref50` and save in the same `{\"ids\",\"emb\"}` `.npy` format as ESM2 outputs. \n- Added `code/AI_CHEM_code/benchmark_with_svr_mlp_balance.py` to run extended benchmarks that include XGBoost, TabPFN (optional), SVR (with LinearSVR fallback for large-N), and MLP baselines, plus quantile-bin balancing experiments and bootstrap-percentile CIs; outputs run-level CSVs and a summary table compatible with existing pipelines. \n- Added `code/AI_CHEM_code/shap_analysis.py` for XGBoost SHAP analyses (summary, dependence plots, global importance, and PCA loading export) and `code/AI_CHEM_code/export_hyperparameter_table.py` plus `code/AI_CHEM_code/build_validation_mutant_table.py` for hyperparameter reporting and collaborator-facing hit/miss tables. \n- Added `code/AI_CHEM_code/REVISION_TASKS.md` with usage examples and updated `env/requirements_main_minimal.txt` to include `transformers` and `shap` for the new tools. \n\n### Testing\n- Performed static syntax checks of all new scripts using `python -m py_compile` and those checks passed for the added files. \n- Attempted to run `export_hyperparameter_table.py` in the current shell which raised `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pandas'` indicating the runtime environment needs the project dependencies installed (expected on a clean environment). \n- No heavy compute runs (full ProtT5 embedding extraction, full cross-model benchmarking, or active-learning reruns) were executed in this PR; the committed scripts are ready to run in the project conda environment or on GPU nodes as described in `REVISION_TASKS.md`.\n\n------\n[Codex Task](https://chatgpt.com/codex/tasks/task_e_699a45d97610832cb921db25f52bc82e)",
